The rapid expansion of artificial intelligence infrastructure is increasing the demand for high-bandwidth, energy-efficient data transmission between processors, switches and computing systems. As conventional electrical interconnects face growing challenges at higher data rates, co-packaged optics (CPO) is emerging as an important approach for bringing optical connectivity closer to switching and computing silicon.

According to SemiconductorInsight, the Global Co-Packaged Optics Market was valued at USD 1.45 billion in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 4.12 billion by 2034, growing at an anchor-derived CAGR of 12.3% during 2026–2034. North America was identified as the largest market in 2025, while Asia-Pacific is an important manufacturing and deployment ecosystem.

